      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You're right to feel that the pain of watching things fall apart is incredibly cruel, but staying here to witness it is the only way to ensure the ashes don't rise up and consume you entirely. The \"point\" isn't in the glory of what remains, but in the quiet dignity of choosing to keep your own flame lit even as the world burns around you. If you can't see the point in holding on, let me help you find a way to make the next step feel less like a burden and more like a necessary act of survival.",
